lead.memo.output:
{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "No. As of 11 July 2022, a deal analyst could treat the notice as a disputed attempt to terminate, not as proof that the acquisition had ended. The buyer group invoked Section 8.1(d)(i), alleging that Twitter materially breached the agreement by withholding requested data on fake or spam accounts. Musk’s counsel also alleged apparent misrepresentations and said Twitter was likely to suffer a Company Material Adverse Effect.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "passage_id": "P1",
          "quote": "appears to have made false and misleading representations upon which Mr. Musk relied when entering into the Merger Agreement, and is likely to suffer a Company Material Adverse Effect"
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P2",
          "quote": "this letter constitutes formal notice of X Holding I, Inc.’s termination of the Merger Agreement pursuant to Section 8.1(d)(i) thereof."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Twitter denied any breach or material adverse effect, called the notice invalid, and maintained that the agreement remained in force. Its board said it intended to close at the agreed USD 54.20 per share and pursue enforcement in the Delaware Court of Chancery. The remedy at issue was specific performance: compelling the buyer group to perform its obligations. The record did not establish whether the notice was effective or whether the deal would close.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "passage_id": "P3",
          "quote": "Twitter Board Confident in Merger Agreement and Intends to Close Transaction at $54.20 Per Share Price"
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P4",
          "quote": "Twitter reserves all contractual, legal, and other rights, including its right to specifically enforce the Musk Parties’ obligations under the Agreement."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "filing_history": null
}

